  "description": "Hand-written meaning annotations for docs/evals/notes-variants-holdout-r7-fixtures.json, written blind to earlier held-out rounds. Terms are lowercase prefixes matched against canonicalized words: number words become digits and ordinal suffixes are dropped. A commitment is mentioned when one verb prefix and one object prefix occur outside a condition span. Condition terms must all occur in the attached condition span. Dates list canonical forms, after any spoken correction; owners and quantities are the final ones after any correction or retraction. key marks a decision or conditional commitment that the prose must state with its condition and date. action marks a commitment that the action list must contain. Statuses list the only status or completion assertions the source makes. labels lists spoken headings or capture labels that name no participant, deliverable or product; a claim may not use a word that occurs only inside one. numbers lists each final quantity (not calendar dates) with the prefixes of the words it is stated with in its own clause, and restriction prefixes a restatement must keep; quantities replaced by a spoken correction are not listed. actors maps each person to the verb prefixes the source makes that person the subject of, including speech acts the person actually made and reported speech; an assignment that was corrected to another person is not listed for the first person. Vendor, product and place names (Hartley, Whitlock, Juniper, Dunmore, Marlow, Harlan, Wren, Brightside, Marlowe, Rosalind, Stanton, Carver, Rowan) are not people and have no actor entry.",
